@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain

-- g5-inspectors.l4: Chapter 5, Subchapter A of the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or
-- Air-Conditioning Systems Law 5785-2025: ss.30 to 32 (authorisation of inspectors, the powers of
-- supervision, and the identification that gates every use of them).
--
-- Written by ENCODER G5.  Imports only prelude, daydate, il-interpretation-time and domain; every fact another
-- group decides is an input (see FRAGMENT-G5.md, "standard inputs").  Hebrew in the quotation comments is
-- copied by script from inputs/law.wiki (srcrefs.py quote); the English is mine.
--
-- How the rules are shaped.
--   * A condition the text lays down as a test ("a person is authorised as inspector only if ...") is a BOOLEAN
--     decision named for its section; the Minister's opinion, the inspector's reason to suppose and the like are
--     INPUTS (fields), never computed.
--   * A power is a MAY rule typed by the party that acts (domain Party) and the act done; its preconditions are
--     the PROVIDED guard, which calls the BOOLEAN decision.  A prohibition (s.32, the proviso of s.31(3)) is a
--     SHANT rule whose guard is the negated condition.  A duty is a MUST rule.
--   * A DEONTIC cannot be compared in #ASSERT, so every test asserts the BOOLEAN decision and the rules are
--     exercised with #TRACE in the tests modules, each trace with its expected result written beside it.
--
-- Periods met here: P22, the period an inspector directs for keeping measurements and tests (s.31(4)).  Kind X
-- (the length is an official's, an input); counted as a duration (kind V): see fork F-P22 in FRAGMENT-G5.md.

§ `Chapter 5, Subchapter A: authorisation of inspectors and powers of supervision`

§§ `Nouns of ss 30 to 32`

-- s.31: the things an inspector may do, one constructor for each, named for the act.
DECLARE `Power of supervision under section 31` IS ONE OF
    `require name, address and identification`            -- s.31(1)
    `require information or a document`                   -- s.31(2)
    `enter a place to supervise`                                       -- s.31(3)
    `make measurements and tests`                         -- s.31(4)
    `order measurements and tests kept`                   -- s.31(4)
    `deal with measurements and tests otherwise`          -- s.31(4)

-- A person the Minister may authorise as an inspector (s.30).  Facts a witness can give; the Minister's opinion
-- and the training and conditions "as the Minister directed" are inputs.
DECLARE `Candidate for authorisation as an inspector` HAS
    `an employee of the Ministry` IS A BOOLEAN                                              -- s.30(a)
    `record of offences` IS A `Record of offences`                                          -- s.30(b)(1), domain
    `in the Minister's opinion an offence of which the candidate was convicted makes him unfit to serve as an inspector` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s.30(b)(1)
    `received the training the Minister directed in the field of the powers he will hold` IS A BOOLEAN                                   -- s.30(b)(2)
    `meets the further conditions of eligibility, if the Minister directed any` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  -- s.30(b)(3); NOTHING if none were directed

-- An inspector at the moment he uses a power: who he is, what the authorisation gave him, and what s.32 asks.
DECLARE `An inspector at work` HAS
    `authorised by the Minister as an inspector under section 30(a)` IS A BOOLEAN       -- s.2 "inspector", s.30(a)
    `powers conferred by the authorisation` IS A LIST OF `Power of supervision under section 31`   -- s.30(a): all or part
    `acting to supervise the implementation of the Law` IS A BOOLEAN                    -- s.31 lead-in
    `performing his function` IS A BOOLEAN                                              -- s.32 lead-in
    `visibly wearing a badge` IS A BOOLEAN                                              -- s.32(1)
    `the badge identifies him and his function` IS A BOOLEAN                            -- s.32(1)
    `holding a certificate signed by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN                         -- s.32(2)
    `the certificate states his function and his powers as an inspector` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s.32(2)
    `the certificate was demanded` IS A BOOLEAN                                         -- s.32(2) "on demand"
    `the certificate was shown on demand` IS A BOOLEAN                                  -- s.32(2); meaningful only if it was demanded
    `the Law has commenced for the work on the system being supervised` IS A BOOLEAN    -- s.63(a), IP2: G7 decides it

-- A place an inspector means to enter (s.31(3)).
DECLARE `Place an inspector means to enter` HAS
    `reason to suppose that a person operating there does work on a cooling system without a licence or not in accordance with the conditions of his licence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reason to suppose that a person operating there engages another in such work without a licence or not in accordance with the conditions of the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `used as a dwelling` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a court order permits the entry` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the holder consented to the entry` IS A BOOLEAN

-- What an inspector demands under s.31(2): information, or a document; "document" includes computer output.
DECLARE `Thing an inspector demands under section 31(2)` IS ONE OF
    `information that is not in a document`
    `a document that is not computer output`
    `computer output as defined in the Computers Law`

DECLARE `Demand under section 31(2)` HAS
    `the inspector demanded it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the thing demanded` IS A `Thing an inspector demands under section 31(2)`
    `the person from whom it was demanded is concerned in the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it secures or eases the implementation of the provisions of the Law` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s.31(4): the period an inspector directs, as he states it (an input; the Law gives no length).
DECLARE `Period an inspector directs for keeping measurements and tests` IS ONE OF
    `a number of days directed for keeping`    HAS `the number of days directed` IS A NUMBER
    `a number of months directed for keeping`  HAS `the number of months directed` IS A NUMBER
    `a number of years directed for keeping`   HAS `the number of years directed` IS A NUMBER
    `a last day directed for keeping`          HAS `the last day directed for keeping` IS A DATE

-- The acts the rules of ss.30 to 32 are about, typed by what is done.
DECLARE `An act under sections 30 to 32` IS ONE OF
    `authorise an employee of the Ministry as an inspector`
        HAS `the candidate authorised` IS A `Candidate for authorisation as an inspector`
            `the powers given` IS A LIST OF `Power of supervision under section 31`
    `publish notice of an inspector's authorisation in Reshumot`
    `use a power of supervision` HAS `the power used` IS A `Power of supervision under section 31`
    `show the certificate signed by the Minister`
    `give what the inspector demanded`

§§ `s 30 -- Authorisation of inspectors`

-- src:248 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} השר יסמיך, מקרב עובדי המשרד, מפקחים שיהיו נתונות להם הסמכויות לפי {{ח:פנימי|פרק ה סימן א|סימן זה}}, כולן או חלקן, לשם פיקוח על ביצוע ההוראות לפי חוק זה.
-- s.30(a) reads "the Minister will authorise" (the verb at src:248), not "may authorise", which this Subchapter uses for
-- discretion (s.36(c), (d); s.39(a)): taken as a DUTY to authorise inspectors from among Ministry employees,
-- with all or some of the Subchapter's powers.  Fork F-DUTY (ss.30(a), 34(a), 36(a)): the power reading follows.
@ref s.30(a) (src:248)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 30 to 32`
`s 30(a) — the Minister shall authorise inspectors from among the employees of the Ministry` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MUST  `authorise an employee of the Ministry as an inspector` authorisee powersGiven
          PROVIDED authorisee's `an employee of the Ministry`

@ref s.30(a) (src:248)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 30 to 32`
`s 30(a), read as a power — the Minister may authorise inspectors from among the employees of the Ministry` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY   `authorise an employee of the Ministry as an inspector` authorisee powersGiven
          PROVIDED authorisee's `an employee of the Ministry`

-- src:249 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} למפקח יוסמך מי שמתקיימים לגביו כל אלה:
-- src:250 | {{ח:תתת|(1)}} הוא לא הורשע בעבירה שמפאת מהותה, חומרתה או נסיבותיה הוא אינו ראוי, לדעת השר, לשמש מפקח;
-- src:251 | {{ח:תתת|(2)}} הוא קיבל הכשרה מתאימה בתחום הסמכויות שיהיו נתונות לו לפי {{ח:פנימי|פרק ה|פרק זה}}, כפי שהורה השר;
-- src:252 | {{ח:תתת|(3)}} הוא עומד בתנאי כשירות נוספים כפי שהורה השר.
-- s.30(b)(1) names no pending-proceedings limb (contrast ss.35(2) and 36(b)(1)): only a conviction.  "Offence"
-- is bare here, where ss.6(a)(3), 21 and 23 say "criminal offence" or "disciplinary offence": taken as a
-- criminal offence (fork F-OFFENCE), the disciplinary reading is the alternative function below.
@ref s.30(b)(1) (src:250)
GIVEN candidate IS A `Candidate for authorisation as an inspector`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 30(b)(1) — the candidate was not convicted of an offence that makes him unfit, in the Minister's opinion` candidate MEANS
    NOT (     candidate's `record of offences`'s `convicted of a criminal offence`
          AND candidate's `in the Minister's opinion an offence of which the candidate was convicted makes him unfit to serve as an inspector` )

@ref s.30(b)(1) (src:250)
GIVEN candidate IS A `Candidate for authorisation as an inspector`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 30(b)(1), counting a conviction for a disciplinary offence too` candidate MEANS
    NOT (     (    candidate's `record of offences`'s `convicted of a criminal offence`
               OR  candidate's `record of offences`'s `convicted of a disciplinary offence` )
          AND candidate's `in the Minister's opinion an offence of which the candidate was convicted makes him unfit to serve as an inspector` )

@ref s.30(b)(2) (src:251)
GIVEN candidate IS A `Candidate for authorisation as an inspector`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 30(b)(2) — the candidate received suitable training, as the Minister directed` candidate MEANS
    candidate's `received the training the Minister directed in the field of the powers he will hold`

-- s.30(b)(3): "as the Minister directed".  Where the Minister directed no further condition there is none to
-- meet, so the limb holds (NOTHING); where he did, it holds only if they are met.
@ref s.30(b)(3) (src:252)
GIVEN candidate IS A `Candidate for authorisation as an inspector`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 30(b)(3) — the candidate meets the further conditions of eligibility the Minister directed` candidate MEANS
    CONSIDER candidate's `meets the further conditions of eligibility, if the Minister directed any`
    WHEN JUST met THEN met
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN TRUE

-- Who may be authorised as an inspector is decided by s.30(a) and (b) TOGETHER: (a) draws the inspectors "from among
-- the employees of the Ministry", and (b) says which of them, by three conditions.  Limb (b) alone does not carry the
-- employee test, so the function below, whose exported name keeps its s.30(b) citation because it is wired by that
-- name, reads the employee limb of (a) first.  Without it a candidate who is not an employee and meets (b)(1) to (3)
-- would be answered TRUE (the defect an independent test author found, fixed after the first deposit).
@ref s.30(a) (src:248)
GIVEN candidate IS A `Candidate for authorisation as an inspector`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 30(a) — the candidate is an employee of the Ministry` candidate MEANS
    candidate's `an employee of the Ministry`

@ref s.30(a), (b) (src:248-252)
@export Whether the Minister may authorise this person as an inspector: he is an employee of the Ministry (s.30(a)), not convicted of an offence that in the Minister's opinion makes him unfit, suitably trained as the Minister directed, and meeting any further conditions the Minister directed (s.30(b)). A person who is not a Ministry employee is never answered TRUE
GIVEN candidate IS A `Candidate for authorisation as an inspector` @desc The person the Minister is considering authorising, with whether he is a Ministry employee and the facts of his record, training and conditions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 30(b) — the candidate may be authorised as an inspector` candidate MEANS
        "(a)" ... `s 30(a) — the candidate is an employee of the Ministry` candidate
    AND "(1)" ... `s 30(b)(1) — the candidate was not convicted of an offence that makes him unfit, in the Minister's opinion` candidate
    AND "(2)" ... `s 30(b)(2) — the candidate received suitable training, as the Minister directed` candidate
    AND "(3)" ... `s 30(b)(3) — the candidate meets the further conditions of eligibility the Minister directed` candidate

-- s.30(a) and (b) say who shall be authorised (src:248, 249): a limit on the Minister, so a prohibition on
-- authorising anyone who is not an employee of the Ministry or who fails a limb of (b).  Its guard is the negated
-- test above, which carries the employee limb; the person is bound from the event.  The rule keeps its name for
-- wiring; "all three conditions" counts (b)'s three, and the employee test of (a) is limb "(a)" of the guard.
@ref s.30(a), (b) (src:248-252)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 30 to 32`
`s 30(b) — the Minister shall authorise as an inspector only a person who satisfies all three conditions` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    SHANT `authorise an employee of the Ministry as an inspector` authorisee powersGiven
          PROVIDED NOT `s 30(b) — the candidate may be authorised as an inspector` authorisee
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "s 30(a), (b): a person who is not an employee of the Ministry, or who fails one of the three conditions, was authorised as an inspector"

-- src:253 | {{ח:תת|(ג)}} הודעה על הסמכת מפקח תפורסם ברשומות.
-- s.30(c) says "notice ... will be published in Reshumot" and names nobody.  An actor is inferred (fork F-ACTOR):
-- the Minister, who made the authorisation.  The party is a parameter, so the other inference is callable.
-- Nothing in ss.30 to 32 makes publication a condition of the authorisation's effect, and none is added.
@ref s.30(c) (src:253)
GIVEN publisher IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 30 to 32`
`s 30(c) — notice of an inspector's authorisation shall be published in Reshumot by` publisher MEANS
    PARTY publisher
    MUST  `publish notice of an inspector's authorisation in Reshumot`

@ref s.30(c) (src:253)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 30 to 32`
`s 30(c) — the Minister shall have notice of an inspector's authorisation published in Reshumot` MEANS
    `s 30(c) — notice of an inspector's authorisation shall be published in Reshumot by` `the Minister`

§§ `s 31 -- Powers of supervision`

-- The inspector holds the power: authorised under s.30(a), the power is among those conferred, he acts for
-- supervision of the Law (s.31 lead-in), and the Law has commenced for the work on the system he supervises (s.63(a);
-- integration point IP2, an input).  The authorising of inspectors in ss.30 is not tied to commencement; only the USE
-- of the powers is.  Whether he may USE the power adds s.32.
-- src:255 | {{ח:סעיף|31|סמכויות פיקוח}}
-- src:256 | {{ח:ת}} לשם פיקוח על ביצוע ההוראות לפי חוק זה, רשאי מפקח –
@ref s.31, s.30(a) (src:255-256)
GIVEN i IS AN `An inspector at work`
      p IS A `Power of supervision under section 31`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the inspector holds the power` i p MEANS
        i's `authorised by the Minister as an inspector under section 30(a)`
    AND elem p (i's `powers conferred by the authorisation`)
    AND i's `acting to supervise the implementation of the Law`
    AND i's `the Law has commenced for the work on the system being supervised`

@ref s.31, s.32 (src:255-256, src:262-265)
@export Whether an inspector may use a given power of supervision: he is authorised with that power, acts to supervise the implementation of the Law, and meets the identification conditions of s.32 (Law ss.30(a), 31, 32)
GIVEN i IS AN `An inspector at work` @desc The inspector and the facts of the occasion: his authorisation, the powers it conferred, whether he is performing his function, wears the badge and holds the certificate
      p IS A `Power of supervision under section 31` @desc The power he means to use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the inspector may use the power` i p MEANS
        `the inspector holds the power` i p
    AND `s 32 — the inspector may use the powers` i

-- src:257 | {{ח:תת|(1)}} לדרוש מכל אדם למסור לו את שמו ומענו ולהציג לפניו תעודת זהות או תעודה רשמית אחרת המזהה אותו;
@ref s.31(1) (src:257)
GIVEN i IS AN `An inspector at work`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 30 to 32`
`s 31(1) — an inspector may require any person to give his name and address and to show identification` i MEANS
    PARTY `an inspector`
    MAY   `use a power of supervision` `require name, address and identification`
          PROVIDED `the inspector may use the power` i `require name, address and identification`

-- src:258 | {{ח:תת|(2)}} לדרוש מכל אדם הנוגע בדבר למסור לו כל ידיעה או מסמך שיש בהם כדי להבטיח או להקל את ביצוען של ההוראות לפי חוק זה; בפסקה זו, ”מסמך“ – לרבות פלט כהגדרתו {{ח:חיצוני|חוק המחשבים|בחוק המחשבים, התשנ״ה–1995}};
-- s.31(2): "document" includes computer output as the Computers Law defines it (src:258).  Information that is not
-- in a document is demandable too; only a DOCUMENT demand is what Third Schedule item (7) prices.
@ref s.31(2) (src:258)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing an inspector demands under section 31(2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 31(2) — the thing is a document, which includes computer output` thing MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `information that is not in a document`           THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a document that is not computer output`                                       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `computer output as defined in the Computers Law` THEN TRUE

@ref s.31(2) (src:258)
GIVEN i IS AN `An inspector at work`
      d IS A `Demand under section 31(2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 31(2) — the demand is one the inspector may make` i d MEANS
        `the inspector may use the power` i `require information or a document`
    AND d's `the person from whom it was demanded is concerned in the matter`
    AND d's `it secures or eases the implementation of the provisions of the Law`

@ref s.31(2) (src:258)
GIVEN i IS AN `An inspector at work`
      d IS A `Demand under section 31(2)`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 30 to 32`
`s 31(2) — an inspector may require a person concerned to give information or a document` i d MEANS
    PARTY `an inspector`
    MAY   `use a power of supervision` `require information or a document`
          PROVIDED `s 31(2) — the demand is one the inspector may make` i d

-- src:724 | {{ח:תת|(7)}} לא מסר מסמך לפי דרישת מפקח שניתנה לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 31|סעיף 31(2)}}.
-- IP10, the interface to G6.  Third Schedule item (7) prices "failing to give a document an inspector demanded
-- under s.31(2)".  A demand counts under s.31(2) only if the inspector could lawfully make it, s.32 included
-- (fork F-ITEM7, reading taken); the alternative that ignores s.32 follows.
@ref s.31(2); Third Schedule item (7) (src:258, src:724)
@export Whether a document was demanded under s.31(2) of the Law, so that failing to give it is the violation of Third Schedule item (7): the inspector demanded a document (not mere information) from a person concerned, and could lawfully do so, including the badge and certificate conditions of s.32
GIVEN i IS AN `An inspector at work` @desc The inspector and the facts of the occasion
      d IS A `Demand under section 31(2)` @desc The demand: what was demanded, from whom, and whether it secures or eases implementation of the Law
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the inspector's demand for a document under s.31(2) was lawfully made` i d MEANS
        d's `the inspector demanded it`
    AND `s 31(2) — the thing is a document, which includes computer output` (d's `the thing demanded`)
    AND `s 31(2) — the demand is one the inspector may make` i d

-- s.31(2) says only that the inspector may "require"; the person's duty to comply is implied by Third Schedule item
-- (7), which prices failing to give a document demanded under it (fork F-COMPLY).  The duty is read as arising only
-- on a demand the inspector could lawfully make.  The text states no time for compliance, so the rule carries none.
@ref s.31(2); Third Schedule item (7) (src:258, src:724)
GIVEN i IS AN `An inspector at work`
      d IS A `Demand under section 31(2)`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 30 to 32`
`s 31(2) — a person concerned shall give the information or document an inspector lawfully demanded` i d MEANS
    IF   d's `the inspector demanded it` AND `s 31(2) — the demand is one the inspector may make` i d
    THEN PARTY `a person`
         MUST  `give what the inspector demanded`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `a person` BECAUSE "s 31(2): the information or document an inspector lawfully demanded was not given"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- IP9, the interface to G6: the violation of Third Schedule item (7), made when a lawful demand for a DOCUMENT was
-- not complied with.  The violator, the reference for the act and the day of the act are facts the caller gives; the
-- text fixes no time for compliance, so when the failure occurred is the caller's fact too.
@ref s.31(2); Third Schedule item (7) (src:258, src:724)
@export The violation committed under Third Schedule item (7) of the Law, if any: a document was lawfully demanded by an inspector under s.31(2) and the person did not give it. Returns the violation for the Chapter 6 sanction, or nothing
GIVEN i IS AN `An inspector at work` @desc The inspector and the facts of the occasion
      d IS A `Demand under section 31(2)` @desc The demand
      violator IS A Person @desc The person who did not give the document
      reference IS A STRING @desc A reference that identifies this act; two violations with the same reference are one act
      dayOfTheAct IS A DATE @desc The day the failure to give the document occurred
      `the person did not give the document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the person did not give the document demanded
GIVETH A MAYBE Violation
`the violation committed under s.31(2), if any` i d violator reference dayOfTheAct `the person did not give the document` MEANS
    IF   `the inspector's demand for a document under s.31(2) was lawfully made` i d AND `the person did not give the document`
    THEN JUST (Violation WITH `the violator` IS violator
                            , `the listed violation` IS `failing to give a document an inspector demanded`
                            , `reference for the act` IS reference
                            , `date of the act` IS dayOfTheAct)
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s.31(2); Third Schedule item (7) (src:258, src:724)
GIVEN i IS AN `An inspector at work`
      d IS A `Demand under section 31(2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 31(2), s 32 ignored — a document was demanded` i d MEANS
        d's `the inspector demanded it`
    AND `s 31(2) — the thing is a document, which includes computer output` (d's `the thing demanded`)
    AND `the inspector holds the power` i `require information or a document`
    AND d's `the person from whom it was demanded is concerned in the matter`
    AND d's `it secures or eases the implementation of the provisions of the Law`

-- src:259 | {{ח:תת|(3)}} להיכנס למקום שיש לו יסוד להניח שפועל בו אדם המבצע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר בלא רישיון או שלא בהתאם לתנאי הרישיון שלו או שאדם מפעיל בו אדם אחר בביצוע עבודה כאמור בלא רישיון או שלא בהתאם לתנאי הרישיון שלו, ובלבד שלא ייכנס למקום המשמש למגורים, אלא על פי צו של בית משפט או בהסכמת המחזיק;
-- s.31(3).  "Has reason to suppose" is the INSPECTOR's belief (contrast s.37(a)(1): the SENIOR inspector's), so it
-- is an input per limb; whether the suspicion proves true is not asked.  The proviso: a dwelling only on a court
-- order or with the holder's consent, the consent having no form (trap T30).
@ref s.31(3) (src:259)
GIVEN place IS A `Place an inspector means to enter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 31(3) — the inspector has reason to suppose that unlicensed or non-conforming work is done or engaged there` place MEANS
        place's `reason to suppose that a person operating there does work on a cooling system without a licence or not in accordance with the conditions of his licence`
    OR  place's `reason to suppose that a person operating there engages another in such work without a licence or not in accordance with the conditions of the licence`

@ref s.31(3) proviso (src:259)
GIVEN place IS A `Place an inspector means to enter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 31(3) proviso — the place may be entered: it is not a dwelling, or a court order permits it, or the holder consented` place MEANS
        (NOT place's `used as a dwelling`)
    OR  place's `a court order permits the entry`
    OR  place's `the holder consented to the entry`

@ref s.31(3) (src:259)
@export Whether an inspector may enter a place: he may use the power to enter, has reason to suppose unlicensed or non-conforming work is done or engaged there, and, if it is a dwelling, has a court order or the holder's consent (Law s.31(3); see s.37(b) for testers and experts)
GIVEN i IS AN `An inspector at work` @desc The inspector and the facts of the occasion
      place IS A `Place an inspector means to enter` @desc The place, whether he has reason to suppose unlicensed work there, whether it is a dwelling, and whether a court order or the holder's consent covers the entry
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` i place MEANS
        `the inspector may use the power` i `enter a place to supervise`
    AND `s 31(3) — the inspector has reason to suppose that unlicensed or non-conforming work is done or engaged there` place
    AND `s 31(3) proviso — the place may be entered: it is not a dwelling, or a court order permits it, or the holder consented` place

@ref s.31(3) (src:259)
GIVEN i IS AN `An inspector at work`
      place IS A `Place an inspector means to enter`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 30 to 32`
`s 31(3) — an inspector may enter a place` i place MEANS
    PARTY `an inspector`
    MAY   `use a power of supervision` `enter a place to supervise`
          PROVIDED `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` i place

@ref s.31(3) proviso (src:259)
GIVEN place IS A `Place an inspector means to enter`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 30 to 32`
`s 31(3) proviso — an inspector shall not enter a dwelling without a court order or the holder's consent` place MEANS
    PARTY `an inspector`
    SHANT `use a power of supervision` `enter a place to supervise`
          PROVIDED NOT `s 31(3) proviso — the place may be entered: it is not a dwelling, or a court order permits it, or the holder consented` place
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `an inspector` BECAUSE "s 31(3) proviso: a dwelling was entered without a court order or the holder's consent"

-- src:260 | {{ח:תת|(4)}} לבצע מדידות ובדיקות, וכן להורות על שמירתן לתקופה שיורה, או לנהוג בהן בדרך אחרת.
@ref s.31(4) (src:260)
GIVEN i IS AN `An inspector at work`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 30 to 32`
`s 31(4) — an inspector may make measurements and tests` i MEANS
    PARTY `an inspector`
    MAY   `use a power of supervision` `make measurements and tests`
          PROVIDED `the inspector may use the power` i `make measurements and tests`

@ref s.31(4) (src:260)
GIVEN i IS AN `An inspector at work`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 30 to 32`
`s 31(4) — an inspector may order measurements and tests kept for a period he directs` i MEANS
    PARTY `an inspector`
    MAY   `use a power of supervision` `order measurements and tests kept`
          PROVIDED `the inspector may use the power` i `order measurements and tests kept`

@ref s.31(4) (src:260)
GIVEN i IS AN `An inspector at work`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 30 to 32`
`s 31(4) — an inspector may deal with measurements and tests in another way` i MEANS
    PARTY `an inspector`
    MAY   `use a power of supervision` `deal with measurements and tests otherwise`
          PROVIDED `the inspector may use the power` i `deal with measurements and tests otherwise`

§§§ `s 31(4) -- the period an inspector directs for keeping (P22)`

-- P22.  The length is the inspector's (kind X): an input, stated as a number of days, months or years counted
-- from the day of the direction, or as a last day.  The end is computed with Interpretation Law s.10(a) for days
-- and s.10(b) for months and years (the module il-interpretation-time).  Kind V (a duration, not a time for
-- doing something): s.10(c) is NOT applied (fork F-P22); the callable alternative applies it.  The day of the
-- direction is itself a day of keeping: s.10(a) leaves it out of the COUNT, not out of the period.
@ref s.31(4) (src:260)
GIVEN direction IS A DATE
      period IS A `Period an inspector directs for keeping measurements and tests`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 31(4) — the last day of the period for keeping directed on` direction period MEANS
    CONSIDER period
    WHEN `a number of days directed for keeping`   n THEN `s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` n `days from` direction
    WHEN `a number of months directed for keeping` n THEN `s 10 — the last day of a period of` n `months from the day` direction
    WHEN `a number of years directed for keeping`  n THEN `s 10 — the last day of a period of` n `years from the day` direction
    WHEN `a last day directed for keeping` lastDay   THEN lastDay

@ref s.31(4) (src:260)
GIVEN direction IS A DATE
      period IS A `Period an inspector directs for keeping measurements and tests`
      cal IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 31(4), s 10(c) applied — the last day of the period for keeping directed on` direction period cal MEANS
    CONSIDER period
    WHEN `a number of days directed for keeping`   n THEN `s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` n `days from` direction `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (cal's `days of rest, recess or holiday`))
    WHEN `a number of months directed for keeping` n THEN `s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` n `months after an event on` direction `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (cal's `days of rest, recess or holiday`))
    WHEN `a number of years directed for keeping`  n THEN `s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` n `years after an event on` direction `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (cal's `days of rest, recess or holiday`))
    WHEN `a last day directed for keeping` lastDay   THEN lastDay

@ref s.31(4) (src:260)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      direction IS A DATE
      period IS A `Period an inspector directs for keeping measurements and tests`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 31(4) — keeping is directed on` day `for a direction given on` direction `and a period of` period MEANS
        day AT LEAST direction
    AND `s 8 — the date` day `is up to and including` (`s 31(4) — the last day of the period for keeping directed on` direction period)

-- Fork F-START (also P23, P24): the other reading begins keeping the day AFTER the direction, the day s.10(a)
-- leaves out of the count being left out of the period as well.
@ref s.31(4) (src:260)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      direction IS A DATE
      period IS A `Period an inspector directs for keeping measurements and tests`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 31(4), beginning the day after the direction — keeping is directed on` day `for a direction given on` direction `and a period of` period MEANS
        day AT LEAST (`s 10 — the first day of a period counted from or after an event on` direction)
    AND `s 8 — the date` day `is up to and including` (`s 31(4) — the last day of the period for keeping directed on` direction period)

§§ `s 32 -- Identification`

-- src:262 | {{ח:סעיף|32|הזדהות}}
-- src:263 | {{ח:ת}} מפקח לא יעשה שימוש בסמכויות הנתונות לו לפי {{ח:פנימי|פרק ה סימן א|סימן זה}} אלא בעת מילוי תפקידו ובהתקיים שניים אלה:
-- src:264 | {{ח:תת|(1)}} הוא עונד באופן גלוי תג המזהה אותו ואת תפקידו;
-- src:265 | {{ח:תת|(2)}} יש בידו תעודה החתומה בידי השר, המעידה על תפקידו ועל סמכויותיו של מפקח, שאותה יציג על פי דרישה.
@ref s.32(1) (src:264)
GIVEN i IS AN `An inspector at work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 32(1) — the inspector visibly wears a badge identifying him and his function` i MEANS
        i's `visibly wearing a badge`
    AND i's `the badge identifies him and his function`

@ref s.32(2) (src:265)
GIVEN i IS AN `An inspector at work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 32(2) — the inspector holds a certificate signed by the Minister stating his function and powers` i MEANS
        i's `holding a certificate signed by the Minister`
    AND i's `the certificate states his function and his powers as an inspector`

-- s.32(2) ends "which he will show on demand".  Read as part of the condition (fork F-DEMAND): an inspector
-- whose certificate was demanded and not shown does not meet limb (2).  Reading A leaves it out.
@ref s.32(2) (src:265)
GIVEN i IS AN `An inspector at work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 32(2) — the certificate, if it was demanded, was shown` i MEANS
    (NOT i's `the certificate was demanded`) OR i's `the certificate was shown on demand`

@ref s.32 (src:263-265)
GIVEN i IS AN `An inspector at work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 32 — the inspector may use the powers` i MEANS
        "lead-in" ... i's `performing his function`
    AND "(1)" ... `s 32(1) — the inspector visibly wears a badge identifying him and his function` i
    AND "(2)" ... `s 32(2) — the inspector holds a certificate signed by the Minister stating his function and powers` i
    AND "(2), on demand" ... `s 32(2) — the certificate, if it was demanded, was shown` i

-- Reading A of s.32(2): the certificate need only be held; showing it on demand is a separate duty (below).
@ref s.32 (src:263-265)
GIVEN i IS AN `An inspector at work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 32, reading A — the inspector may use the powers, showing the certificate on demand being a separate duty` i MEANS
        "lead-in" ... i's `performing his function`
    AND "(1)" ... `s 32(1) — the inspector visibly wears a badge identifying him and his function` i
    AND "(2)" ... `s 32(2) — the inspector holds a certificate signed by the Minister stating his function and powers` i

-- "An inspector shall not use the powers ... except ..." is a prohibition: SHANT, guarded by the negated test.
-- The power used is a wildcard, so the prohibition reaches every power of the Subchapter.
@ref s.32 (src:263-265)
GIVEN i IS AN `An inspector at work`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 30 to 32`
`s 32 — an inspector shall not use the powers unless he is performing his function, wears the badge and holds the certificate` i MEANS
    PARTY `an inspector`
    SHANT `use a power of supervision` powerInQuestion
          PROVIDED NOT `s 32 — the inspector may use the powers` i
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `an inspector` BECAUSE "s 32: an inspector used a power without performing his function, or without the badge, or without the certificate"

-- The duty that accompanies limb (2): show the certificate on demand.  Reading A makes it the whole of the
-- "on demand" words; reading B keeps it too (an inspector who refuses has also failed the condition).
@ref s.32(2) (src:265)
GIVEN i IS AN `An inspector at work`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 30 to 32`
`s 32(2) — an inspector whose certificate is demanded shall show it` i MEANS
    IF   i's `the certificate was demanded`
    THEN PARTY `an inspector`
         MUST  `show the certificate signed by the Minister`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `an inspector` BECAUSE "s 32(2): the certificate was demanded and not shown"
    ELSE FULFILLED
